WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.127
This query groups the sales source by product and month.

00:00:03.127 --> 00:00:07.847
COUNT tells us how many transaction rows exist in each product-month group.

00:00:07.847 --> 00:00:11.577
SUM shows the total revenue that would fill a pivot cell.

00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:15.182
Look for groups where source rows is greater than one.

00:00:15.182 --> 00:00:18.837
Those groups prove that the pivot requires aggregation.

00:00:18.837 --> 00:00:24.212
Reshaping can change grain, so define it before and after the transformation.

00:00:24.212 --> 00:00:30.752
A source may have one row per patient-measurement, while a pivoted result has one row per patient.

00:00:30.752 --> 00:00:36.707
If multiple source rows map to the same target cell, you must decide how they are aggregated;

00:00:36.707 --> 00:00:38.983
otherwise information can be lost.
